review:
This is one of the most influential games ever created, as it set the standard for every other over-the-shoulder third-person game that came after, and it aged like fine wine.

[b]Pros:[/b]
• Engaging gameplay with a unique inventory management system;
• Perfect characteristic Japanese horror atmosphere from the PS2/GameCube era, built from incredible visuals (art style) and sound design;
• Memorable soundtrack that complements the visual style and sets the mood masterfully;
• Awesome protagonists and villains;
• OG Leon is the best iteration of the character by far, from his voice acting to his personality;
• One-liners and dialogue are exclusive to cutscenes, making them feel even more rewarding;
• The transformations for bosses are very well made;
• The full-of-personality, stylized UI;
• Splash art in end-chapter screens and notes found in the game;
• Cool alternative unlockable outfits;
• Extra game modes were released as part of the base game;

[b]Cons:[/b]
• These older games make me realize they don't do it like they used to and that video games are not catered to the same audience anymore.

With this said, this is the definitive experience and one that I thoroughly recommend.

It's good. Not "OMG this is AMAZING!!!" as some fanboys would like you you think, but good nonetheless. Also, unlike previous installments, this is not a horror game. It's more of a horror-themed action game. 
[b]Pros:[/b]
* Solid action gameplay;
* Free aiming and limb targeting system is cool;
* Good selection of upgradable weapons;
* Plenty of unlockables for completionists;
* With HD Project mod installed it looks amazing, nothing like a GameCube or a PS2 game.
[b]Cons:[/b]
* Horror is pretty much non-existent;
* Controls can be clunky (you cannot strafe);
* Puzzles are a joke;
* Some cheap QTEs in the middle of cutscenes catch you unawares;
* No ammo or healing scarcity;
* FOV is absolute ass, can't see sh*t (fixable by RE4 tweaks, a must-have mod);
* The story, dialog, and overall writing quality are terrible;
* By the end gets somewhat repetitive.
[b]Overall:[/b] by the standards of 2005 it's a very good game. But in 2022 it's far from being "the best Resident Evil game" like some rabid fanboys would like you to think.

