Originally released for the Nintendo GameCube in 2005, this is a classic game and one of the best of its time. While many may think that this game is dated because of the clunky characters and controls, this is not entirely true. The game was designed to have characters that feel heavy to give a more survival type of gameplay instead of pure action. This port is keyboard and mouse compatible and aiming feels much more fluid compared to the PS2 port. While this port could have been better optimized for PC and the remaster could have higher quality textures by Capcom, this is still a great game to play and own.

If you buy this game, make sure to check out the RE4HD Project Mod. This is a must.
https://steamcommunity.com/app/254700/discussions/0/558749824370582987/

[u]Pros[/u]
+ Keyboard and mouse compatibillity;
+ It has a fairly good modding community;
+ The game has a very nice horror atmosphere;
+ It blends action and survival horror very well;
+ The longest campaign in the franchise with many hours of gameplay, plus the bonuses.

[u]Cons[/u]
- It doesn't have sound configuration in the menu;
- You can't use your mouse in the inventory;
- There's only a few achievements;
- The Mercenaries Mode does not have Leaderboards;
- Some quick time events for keyboard are on buttons X+C, which are terrible;
- This Las Plagas and Illuminados bs is just insanely dumb.

